# Bash macros

Prefixes → [naming.mdc](naming.mdc). Bundle layout: [../../../scripts/bash_macros/README.md](../../../scripts/bash_macros/README.md).

Applies to projects with `scripts/bash_macros/` and `load_macros`. Public macros (`build`, `diag`, `load_macros`) — **no** prefix.

## Namespace — do not duplicate the bundle name

`_macros_bind_namespace` turns function `name` into `namespace::name`. If the helper is `_diag_search`, the API is `diag::_diag_search`.

```bash
# Bad — double prefix
_diag_search_something() { ... }
_macros_bind_namespace diag _diag_search_something
# → diag::_diag_search_something

# Good — the namespace already provides context
_search_something() { ... }
_macros_bind_namespace diag _search_something
# → diag::_search_something
```

The function name **must not** include the bundle name (`diag`, `build`, `load`, `tr`, …) — the namespace already adds it in the public API.
